= Inference — Simple =

'''Inference''' means reaching a conclusion from other information.

Example:

<pre>
All mammals are animals.
Whales are mammals.
Therefore whales are animals.
</pre>

That is a deductive inference.

Other kinds include:

* '''induction''' — use examples to make a broader conclusion;
* '''abduction''' — choose a plausible explanation;
* '''probabilistic inference''' — update probabilities.

A valid deduction guarantees the conclusion only if the premises are true.

Computers can also make inferences from [[Knowledge representation/Simple|knowledge representations]].

For example, if an ontology says every Dog is a Mammal and Fido is a Dog, a reasoner can infer that Fido is a Mammal.

